## Scope: the MIT grant above covers this plugin's original code only

Code licensing and data licensing are separate. This plugin ships a bundled data
asset and depends on third-party software. Neither is relicensed by the grant
above:

- **The bundled reference database** — `src/providers/ocl/nmrshiftdb2.database.json`,
  and the built `assets/nmrWorker-*.js` chunk that embeds it — is a **derivative
  database** under the **nmrshiftdb2 Database License** (ODbL-derived). It permits
  use including commercial use, but carries **share-alike and attribution**
  obligations that travel with any redistribution — including redistribution of a
  packaged `.zip` of this plugin, which contains that database. See
  `src/providers/ocl/NMRSHIFTDB2_LICENSE.md` for the provenance record and the
  upstream license text, which governs.

- **Third-party dependencies** — openchemlib (BSD-3-Clause), zod (MIT) — remain
  under their own terms. See `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`.

Nothing in the MIT grant above conveys any right to those materials beyond their
respective licenses.

MIT was chosen deliberately rather than as a default: the nmrshiftdb2 Database
License requires that prediction software relying on the database be under an
OSI-approved license. MIT is OSI-approved and satisfies that condition.
